{
  "requirement": "The enabled Habeas Symposium plugin MUST request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI and use that installation as its session-start hook command, so the CLI is available when the hook advises an agent to run `habeas setup`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The one marked test, `tests/repository.rs#fn[symposium_plugin_installs_the_cli_globally_for_its_session_start_hook]`, adequately checks `requirements.integration.symposium_cli`. It parses the real `Cargo.toml` through `repository_toml` and asserts on `package.metadata.symposium`.\n\nThe requirement has these obligations, each mapped to an assertion:\n- **Request a Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI.** The test asserts there is exactly one installation. It asserts `source == \"cargo\"`, `crate == \"habeas\"` and `executable == \"habeas\"`.\n- **Make the installation global.** The test asserts `global == true`. A non-global or missing flag would fail it.\n- **Use that installation as the session-start hook command.** The test asserts there is exactly one hook. It asserts `event == \"SessionStart\"`. It asserts `hooks[0][\"command\"]` equals `installation[\"executable\"]`, so the hook command is tied to the installed executable rather than a separate literal.\n- **The hook advises running `habeas setup`.** The test asserts the hook args are `[\"hook\", \"session-start\"]`. What the hook outputs belongs to other requirements, such as `requirements.integration.symposium_setup_hook`, and is outside this subject.\n\nThe requirement does not distinguish other input classes. \"Enabled\" describes the plugin's metadata being present in `Cargo.toml`. It is not a separate mode with its own behavior to test. No acknowledgments apply, and I found no marking gap.",
  "references": "fa2249c214e538b1c0cfce0d46ee53e74a6358578cf17a615dadfcc6e43ab2dc",
